{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993634660299001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"spiny-micro-ladle","assignee":"Joe Oakhart","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"b798898502f6a6d107abe32d28ca25f85e91db8d","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 4e82-6034-6d5a-4d39","material: 469316b6062f9982","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 15","regver: 83e5f63ad06d893a","verified-at-sha:cea18e2dbcad4d164aaa9dbc48fe0e90edf37c1d","dep absent docs/adr/0010-gerrit-github-replication.md","dep absent infra/gerrit/replication.config","dep absent infra/gerrit/setup-replication.sh","dep absent infra/terraform/monitoring_s5.tf"],"signature":"55642f1add85255b1d868f6589259f7caa8dc83b8bbc580e91f3e0fab1c9e393","signed_at":1782791756028239000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":22},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"DERISK (E5): replication identity = a single-repo WRITE deploy key. navapbc/rebar currently has 0 deploy keys; S5 adds the key (private half in SSM) and S6 bypass-lists it. Replication plugin authenticates via passwordless SSH public key (per docs) — matches the deploy-key approach.","timestamp":1782686147925115001},{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"## S5 implemented + verified LIVE — 2026-06-30 (commit dd36a3750)\n\nReplication plugin (bundled) configured + deploy key live. navabpc/rebar main UNCHANGED at cea18e2 throughout (no real-main advance — that is S7's e2e).\n\n**AC verification (subagent + alarm test, all PASS):**\n- AC1 — Replication push works: replication_log shows `Push to ...rebar.git ... refs/heads/main:refs/heads/main force=no ... 0 retries`; a tag pushed to Gerrit replicated to GitHub (`git ls-remote` showed gerrit-repl-smoke=cea18e2), then deleted from both (cleanup confirmed).\n- AC2 — projects=rebar binding: only `rebar` replicates (config + log show only `rebar:` scheduling).\n- AC3 — refs/changes/* + refs/meta/config NOT pushed: `git ls-remote github | grep refs/changes|refs/meta` empty.\n- AC4 — mirror=false, replicationMaxRetries=3, timeout=60.\n- AC5 — `[replication] eventsDirectory=data/replication`; /var/gerrit/data/replication exists (crash-safe queue).\n- AC6 — NON-FORCE enforced: forced Gerrit main to a divergent root; replication returned `REJECTED_NONFASTFORWARD`; **GitHub main stayed cea18e2 (unchanged)**. Gerrit main restored.\n- AC7 — deploy key on disk: /var/gerrit/.ssh/id_ed25519 mode 0600 owner uid 1000; ~/.ssh/config routes github.com to it.\n- AC8 — fail-closed: materialize-deploy-key.sh with a bogus SSM param exits non-zero (ParameterNotFound), writes no key.\n- AC9 — `ssh -T git@github.com` (as gerrit user) -> \"Hi navapbc/rebar! You've successfully authenticated\".\n- AC10 — reproducible as-code: register-deploy-key.sh + materialize-deploy-key.sh + setup-replication.sh + replication.config (idempotent).\n- AC11 — replication-failure ALERT fires: CloudWatch alarm `rebar-gerrit-replication-errors` on `rebar/host:replication_errors`; the observability probe detected the AC6 non-FF line and published the metric -> alarm transitioned OK -> ALARM (verified); recovered to OK after a 0 datapoint.\n- AC12 — kill-switch <5min: `mv replication.config aside` + restart -> \"not replicating\"; restored -> \"Succeeded! (OK)\".\n- ADR-0010 committed (one-way-door contract, BSL note, rotation, kill-switch).\n\n**Deploy key:** registered on navapbc/rebar (write-enabled, id 155914477), private key from SSM /rebar/prod/github-replication-deploy-key.\n**NOTE for S7:** admin cannot direct-push to refs/heads/main (review-gated, by design) — the real-main advance e2e must go through the review/submit flow (or a deliberate temp ACL).\n\n**Code review (subagent):** VERDICT was CHANGES-REQUESTED for 1 blocker — observability.sh `grep -c || echo 0` corrupted the count on the healthy zero-failure path. FIXED (drop `|| echo 0`, `total=${total:-0}`); redeployed + verified clean (total=1 single line, new=0, publishes 0). NITs (ssh-keyscan TOFU; dimension-contract comment) addressed/noted.","timestamp":1782793375025816001}],"created_at":1782685506045700001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e0e86310-0822-42bd-a023-9c388117edec","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a88d-bc7e-728b-42b6"}],"description":"# S5 — Gerrit -> GitHub one-way replication (core plugin, non-force, deploy key)\n\n## Why\nMake Gerrit the sole writer of GitHub `main`. The core, Apache-2.0, WAR-bundled `replication`\nplugin (push) is the right tool — the GerritForge BSL re-license (2025-09-30) touched only\n`pull-replication`/multi-site, not this plugin. The non-force / `mirror=false` / deploy-key\nchoices form a one-way-door replication contract (Gerrit is the only writer; GitHub history is\nappend-only/fast-forward), captured as an ADR (## Files).\n\n## What\n- `replication.config` (`infra/gerrit/replication.config`):\n  - `url = git@github.com:navapbc/rebar.git` (scp-style SSH).\n  - **`projects = rebar`** (peer-pattern correction — REQUIRED). Because the URL\n    hardcodes the single repo and uses no `${name}` interpolation, WITHOUT a `projects =`\n    filter the remote matches **every** Gerrit project and tries to push each one's `main`+tags\n    into the one GitHub repo. Bind it to exactly the `rebar` project.\n  - `push = refs/heads/main:refs/heads/main` + `push = refs/tags/*:refs/tags/*` (NON-force — no\n    leading `+`).\n  - `mirror=false` (true does a destructive prune of remote refs absent/invisible locally).\n  - `replicatePermissions=false` (don't leak `refs/meta/config`); explicit refspecs so\n    `refs/changes/*` is never pushed.\n  - finite `replicationMaxRetries = 3`; `timeout = 60` (seconds). Values are concrete; they may\n    be tuned but must remain finite/bounded — unlimited retries are forbidden (see AC).\n- **Crash-safe queue (peer-pattern correction).** Set `[replication] eventsDirectory =\n  data/replication` in the plugin's own `replication.config` (NOT `gerrit.config`, where the\n  replication plugin silently ignores it) so pending replication\n  events survive a Gerrit restart. Without it, the push queue is in-memory and a restart\n  mid-queue silently drops pending pushes, leaving the GitHub mirror stale.\n- Identity: a single-repo, write-enabled, passphrase-less GitHub deploy key on `navapbc/rebar`\n  (currently **0 deploy keys** — S5 adds exactly one; GitHub-side bypass-listing is S6's job).\n  Private key from **SSM Parameter Store** at `/rebar/prod/github-deploy-key` (SecureString).\n  The replication plugin's SSH client runs as the **Gerrit OS user** (`gerrit2`), so the key +\n  SSH config live in `/home/gerrit2/.ssh/`, not root's.\n- Provisioning is **as-code and idempotent**: the GitHub deploy-key registration + SSM parameter\n  are managed by IaC (Terraform `github_repository_deploy_key` + `aws_ssm_parameter`, or an\n  equivalent checked-in idempotent script), and an init/entrypoint hook materialises the key from\n  SSM + seeds `known_hosts` **before** the replication plugin can fire its first push.\n- **SSM->disk materialisation + ordering (the most common failure mode):** an entrypoint step,\n  run as/writing to `gerrit2` and ordered **before** Gerrit's main process starts, must: (1)\n  `aws ssm get-parameter --name /rebar/prod/github-deploy-key --with-decryption` -> write\n  `/home/gerrit2/.ssh/id_ed25519` owned by `gerrit2`, mode `0600`; (2) `ssh-keyscan github.com\n  >> /home/gerrit2/.ssh/known_hosts` (non-interactive first connection); (3) write `~/.ssh/config`\n  `Host github.com` with `IdentityFile` pointing at that key. This step **MUST hard-fail\n  (fail-closed):** on ANY `aws ssm get-parameter` failure (throttle, IAM-propagation lag,\n  network-not-ready) or a missing/empty key value it **exits non-zero and ABORTS Gerrit startup**\n  — never continue and let Gerrit start without the deploy key, since that yields silent\n  replication failure rather than a loud one.\n- **Lifecycle / rotation (one-way-door — in the ADR):** rotation = generate new keypair -> add\n  the new GitHub deploy key -> update SSM -> reload the replication plugin -> remove the old key\n  (no outage gap). Reproducible from checked-in IaC.\n- **Observability:** a persistent alert (not just the one-time check) on `replication_log`\n  ERROR / max-retry-exhaustion / `REJECTED_NONFASTFORWARD` — a log-based metric + alarm so\n  operators are notified when replication stalls (revoked key, network partition, non-FF\n  rejection) instead of GitHub silently going stale.\n- **Rollback / kill-switch:** replication disabled in <5 min without a full redeploy by renaming\n  the config + reloading the plugin (`mv replication.config replication.config.disabled && ssh\n  -p 29418 <gerrit> gerrit plugin reload replication`); if the key is suspected compromised,\n  revoke the GitHub deploy key + rotate SSM.\n\n## Scope\nIn: replication plugin config (incl. `projects=` + crash-safe `eventsDirectory`) + the\ndeploy-key identity (SSM->disk, `~/.ssh/config`, `known_hosts`) + as-code provisioning + push of\n`main`+tags + replication-failure alerting + a documented rollback/kill-switch + the ADR. Out:\nthe GitHub-side lockdown that makes the mirror read-only (S6). **S5->S6 ordering (do not\nignore):** S5 turns on non-force push **before** S6 forbids direct GitHub writes, so a direct\npush to GitHub `main` in that window would diverge it and cause every subsequent non-force\nreplication to be rejected `non-fast-forward`. Mitigate by (a) deploying S6 in the same\nchange-set or promptly after, AND (b) the pre-activation prerequisite + non-FF alert below.\n\n### Pre-activation prerequisite\nBefore enabling replication, verify GitHub `main` is fast-forwardable from Gerrit's HEAD:\n`git ls-remote https://github.com/navapbc/rebar refs/heads/main` HEAD must be an ancestor of (or\nequal to) Gerrit's `main` HEAD. If GitHub is already ahead, resolve the divergence first.\n\n## Files\n- `infra/gerrit/replication.config` — push refspecs, `projects=`, `mirror=false`,\n  `replicatePermissions=false`, finite retries, timeout.\n- `infra/gerrit/replication.config` — holds the ENTIRE replication config: `[remote \"github\"]` (url, non-force push refspecs, `replicatePermissions=false`), `projects=rebar`, AND `[replication] eventsDirectory = data/replication`. (NOT `gerrit.config` — the plugin reads only its own `replication.config`.)\n- `infra/gerrit/entrypoint.sh` (or init hook) — SSM->disk key materialisation + `ssh-keyscan`\n  known_hosts + `~/.ssh/config`, run as `gerrit2` before Gerrit starts.\n- `infra/` deploy-key provisioning as-code — Terraform `github_repository_deploy_key` +\n  `aws_ssm_parameter` (SecureString at `/rebar/prod/github-deploy-key`) or a checked-in\n  idempotent script; includes teardown.\n- `infra/` replication-failure alert definition (log-based metric + alarm on `replication_log`\n  ERROR / max-retry / `REJECTED_NONFASTFORWARD`).\n- `docs/adr/0010-gerrit-github-replication.md` — ADR: plugin choice + BSL rationale, non-force /\n  fast-forward-only policy, `mirror=false`, `projects=` single-repo binding, crash-safe\n  `eventsDirectory`, deploy-key rotation lifecycle, and the pointer to S6.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A change submitted in Gerrit replicates `main` to `navapbc/rebar` (non-force, fast-forward)\n      and tags replicate, verified by `replication_log` exit-0 + `git ls-remote` reflecting the SHA.\n- [ ] The remote is bound via `projects = rebar` so ONLY the rebar project replicates\n      to the GitHub repo (no other Gerrit project is pushed there), verified by config + log.\n- [ ] `refs/changes/*` and `refs/meta/config` are NOT pushed to GitHub (explicit refspecs +\n      `replicatePermissions=false`), verified by inspecting GitHub refs after replication.\n- [ ] `mirror=false` (no destructive pruning) and `replicationMaxRetries` is finite (e.g. 3,\n      never unlimited) with a bounded `timeout`.\n- [ ] `[replication] eventsDirectory` is set so the replication queue is crash-safe across a\n      Gerrit restart (a restart mid-queue does not silently drop pending pushes).\n- [ ] **Non-force is enforced end-to-end:** given a GitHub `main` that cannot be fast-forwarded,\n      the push is **rejected** — `replication_log` records `non-fast-forward` (exit non-zero) and\n      GitHub history is **unchanged** (guards against a stray `+`).\n- [ ] The replication identity is a single-repo write deploy key whose private key is from SSM\n      (no plaintext in VCS); on the host `/home/gerrit2/.ssh/id_ed25519` exists owned by\n      `gerrit2` mode `0600`, `~/.ssh/config` routes `github.com` to it, `known_hosts` pre-seeded.\n- [ ] **The entrypoint SSM-materialisation step hard-fails (fail-closed):** simulating an `aws\n      ssm get-parameter` failure (or a missing/empty key) causes the step to exit non-zero and\n      Gerrit **does not start** — Gerrit never comes up without the replication deploy key.\n- [ ] A pre-activation SSH smoke-test passes before go-live: `sudo -u gerrit2 ssh -T\n      git@github.com` returns GitHub's \"successfully authenticated\" banner (no host-key prompt).\n- [ ] Deploy-key + SSM provisioning is reproducible as-code (re-run on a clean host recreates\n      key + SSM param + on-disk key + known_hosts, no manual steps); teardown documented.\n- [ ] A persistent replication-failure alert fires (in a test) on an ERROR / max-retry /\n      `non-fast-forward` entry in `replication_log`, so a silent stall in the S5->S6 window is caught.\n- [ ] A rollback/kill-switch works: replication disabled in <5 min via `mv replication.config\n      replication.config.disabled` + `gerrit plugin reload replication`, with deploy-key\n      revocation as the compromise path.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0010-gerrit-github-replication.md` captures the replication-contract decisions.\n\n## Round-7 remediation\n- **Concrete project name (E2):** `projects = rebar` (the project S3 creates on the Gerrit instance) — not a placeholder.\n\n## Round-8 remediation\n- **eventsDirectory location (G6):** `[replication] eventsDirectory = data/replication` belongs in `replication.config` (the replication plugin's OWN config file), NOT `gerrit.config` (Gerrit silently ignores the unknown stanza there). Place it in `infra/gerrit/replication.config`.\n\n## Plan-review remediation (Round-11, 2026-06-29)\n- BSL scope RESOLVED (Round-12): GerritForge's 2025-09-30 re-license (gitenterprise.me/2025/09/30/re-licensing-gerritforge-plugins-welcome-to-gerrit-enterprise) moved the **pull-replication** and **multi-site** GerritForge plugins to BSL (their Apache-2.0 versions deprecated). The **core `replication` (push) plugin used here ships with Gerrit Core under Apache-2.0** — GerritForge explicitly keeps the widely-used/core plugins Apache-2.0. This epic uses push `replication`, NOT pull-replication or multi-site, so it is unaffected. No legal review needed at build; ADR-0010 records this citation + a 1-line LICENSE-string check of the bundled `replication` jar in the pinned 3.14.1 image as the mechanical confirmation.\n\nAdded ACs:\n- [ ] ADR-0010 cites the BSL re-license scope (or records the LICENSE-in-image verification) confirming the `replication` push plugin used here is Apache-2.0, not BSL-restricted","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/gerrit/replication.config","reason":"replication plugin remote github: url, refspecs, replicatePermissions=false, projects=rebar, eventsDirectory"},{"path":"infra/gerrit/setup-replication.sh","reason":"install replication.config + register deploy key + known_hosts; trigger replication"},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_s5.tf","reason":"CloudWatch alarm on replication failures"},{"path":"docs/adr/0010-gerrit-github-replication.md","reason":"ADR replication design + BSL license note"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a88d-bc7e-728b-42b6"],["parent","d251-05e1-eb55-43b2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d251-05e1-eb55-43b2","parent_status_uuid":"a5dd17df-decf-4fb1-b13a-11a1404a01e3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["gerrit","github","replication"],"ticket_id":"4e82-6034-6d5a-4d39","ticket_type":"story","title":"infra: S5 — Gerrit->GitHub one-way replication (core plugin, non-force, deploy key)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a70122c8-8c42-4ea9-8edf-42823077e0e8","e0e86310-0822-42bd-a023-9c388117edec","40a3aca0-a346-4ee8-957e-405255631be1","f3297e3e-7cea-4462-9809-17a7a0b7071b","159042fe-e6fd-45ea-b7db-fb790c47cb68","349364b1-6159-48fd-9b80-a31e41f255bd","0fec89cd-59da-4e3c-ba1a-b4a8aa5a6b16","0459f8dd-52ef-44ca-8ec3-749335589042","19b1d8e0-de71-4733-bd2a-5a0e43168274","32499e35-a62a-4741-b81a-1c9887a30a78","c2c0233d-69c9-440b-9177-64e4b0eaf2ad","8138cae9-0fc5-4f96-bc72-85a982097a42","6db7e0ae-43ac-4054-bd22-9a616371b46c","dedfbb13-ced8-4c7e-a4a0-c53ca8eec463","ad3fcc4b-52c1-47b7-9ef2-b1f108297ead","41ca5466-7af7-466a-9026-674fce763cd0","4ee0e29e-b3f8-426b-bca8-d790daedb6ba","e16c369a-e675-49e1-9842-d76a50fa4810","da366965-96ab-47e0-8f09-1ba732508472","d1f3fe1b-39e6-4ce3-a6d4-d6132745393d","70b6729b-4f67-46eb-adf4-2b8592387520","858883e6-a73a-4a83-966c-a6715a1a9592","4061820f-157e-453f-af75-eb08e3b5b26e","58688ec4-347e-4ee9-8f0f-a7f82254e4a9","7818a596-0626-4760-ac9d-ac0823d66666","f97758bf-62b1-486c-9e82-b0561f1b0940","4db67abd-f063-4407-a8ff-24d1d59bfa20","06ec3d37-0f52-49e3-b052-060b143119fa","dec0548e-7baf-4540-8904-736dbac831a2","a5dd17df-decf-4fb1-b13a-11a1404a01e3","edff85eb-af5d-4858-8938-3fdf91cea286","538a0e62-6d84-406a-bde6-ffa5111d512a","819a980f-f904-4b14-bd04-7a986817b5e2"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993634660299001,"uuid":"b0b24523-7635-4dd4-a3be-b3ebbfea50e4"}